{
  "id": "27014_miwaku",
  "headword": "{魅惑|みわく}",
  "reading": "みわく",
  "romaji": "miwaku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "fascination; charm; enchantment",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "fascination; charm; enchantment; allure",
      "explanation": "A captivating or bewitching quality that draws people in."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27014_miwaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{魅惑|みわく}の{歌声|うたごえ}。",
      "english": "An enchanting singing voice.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27014_miwaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}の{魅惑|みわく}に{抗|あらが}えなかった。",
      "english": "I couldn't resist her charm.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27014_miwaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{街|まち}には{旅行者|りょこうしゃ}を{引|ひ}きつける{魅惑|みわく}がたくさんある。",
      "english": "This city has many charms that attract travelers.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Describes a captivating, almost spellbinding quality. The kanji {魅|み} means 'bewitch' and {惑|わく} means 'confuse/beguile,' giving the word a sense of irresistible, almost dangerous allure. Often used as a modifier in the pattern {魅惑|みわく}の + noun.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {魅惑|みわく}の{世界|せかい}: an enchanting world\n- {魅惑|みわく}の{笑顔|えがお}: a captivating smile\n- {魅惑|みわく}する: to fascinate; to enchant\n- {魅惑|みわく}に{満|み}ちた: full of charm\n- {魅惑|みわく}{的|てき}な: fascinating; alluring\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {魅力|みりょく}: charm; appeal — more neutral and broadly used; does not carry the same sense of bewitchment\n- {誘惑|ゆうわく}: temptation; seduction — implies actively luring someone, often with negative connotations\n- {妖艶|ようえん}: bewitchingly beautiful — limited to describing sensual or mysterious beauty",
